      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs are in that familiar late-September place - not yet judged, but already getting sorted out. <strong>The real headline is the club's visit to Matthew Mayich's family in the hospital before practice in Arizona</strong>, a gesture that says as much about the room as any exhibition score ever could. Toronto's preseason has been uneven - a 6-1 win over Ottawa after a pair of losses to Montreal - but those results only matter as seasoning, not judgment. The bigger story is the new look in goal and the roster squeeze, with cuts and waivers trimming the fat while the staff tests who can survive when the games count. <strong>Tuesday's regular-season opener against Montreal will tell us whether the new backbone holds or the old Leaf fragility creeps back in.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
