      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The curtain is falling on a season that went nowhere fast - and Toronto at least gets one last theater piece before the lights go out. <strong>Max Scherzer is slated to start the finale against the Reds, with his future still undecided</strong>, and that's the right final image for a club that is 78-83, fifth in the AL East, and already finished in the standings. Friday's 5-1 loss to Cincinnati underlined the gap; the Jays salvaged one game with a 6-5 win on Thursday, then stumbled again. Now the clubhouse turns to auditions and honesty. Trey Yesavage's brief cameo was a small signpost, and the young arms and bats getting these last looks matter more than the box score. <strong>After Sunday, the real work begins - deciding which kids stay, which veterans go, and how to fix a roster that never found its spine</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
