        "body": "The offense has gone from promising to precarious in a hurry - and the bruise on the forehead is the quarterback room. <strong>Jayden Daniels is out for Week 3 with an elbow injury, and Marcus Mariota is back under center</strong>, which is the sort of sentence that tells you exactly where this season stands in late September. At 0-2, fourth in the NFC East and already two games back, Washington can't afford more self-inflicted wounds after the 37-20 loss to Dallas. Daniels' absence is the story, not the footnote; his health now matters as much as the standings. Mariota has to steady a team that is already chasing. <strong>Sunday's test against the Seahawks is about survival, composure and whether this club can stop hemorrhaging losses before October arrives.</strong>",
