  "morning_brief": {
    "article": {
      "title": "Leafs, Jays, and a Sunday test",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Maple Leafs are in Arizona with a simple eye on Tuesday night, when they host the Canadiens in their season opener on Sportsnet. Before practice, the team visited Matthew Mayich's family at the hospital in a gesture that has become the warmest note of camp.",
        "The Blue Jays close the book today at 3:07 p.m. ET against the Reds on Sportsnet, with Max Scherzer set to start opposite Brandon Williamson. Toronto fell 5-1 last night, and Scherzer said he will decide in the offseason whether to retire.",
        "The Raptors are back in training camp with their preseason date against the Heat on Oct. 3 and their regular-season opener against the Bulls on Oct. 21. In Washington, the Commanders host the Seahawks at 1 p.m. ET on FOX, and Marcus Mariota gets the start with Jayden Daniels out."
      ]
